Native Go routing dependency for the installed notification plugins.

Reference: requests 2.34.2 (Apache 2.0; licenses/Requests-Apache-2.0.txt)
and the original NAS CPython 3.12.13 urllib.request environment functions
(PSF; licenses/CPython-PSF.txt). The original source hashes and read-only Linux
capture are retained with the source comparison evidence.

The existing Resolve explicit MoviePilot PROXY mapping remains separate.
The native environment resolver covers the tested Linux trust-env path;
it does not read macOS SystemConfiguration or Windows registry proxy settings.
The original NAS is Linux. Python is used only for offline source comparison;
the Go product and its tests do not invoke Python or the original plugins.

HTTP and SOCKS wire tests use owned local listeners only. Request context is
explicitly retained through proxy handshakes, preserving caller TLS settings.
Errors do not print proxy credential values. Callers retain authorization of
target origins, redirects and credentials; this package is only transport.

SOCKS4/4a reference additionally reviewed against the original installed
PySocks 1.7.1 source; its BSD license is retained (licenses/PySocks-BSD.txt).
Legacy numeric IPv4 is encoded as an address, and other SOCKS4a destinations
are sent as remote names, including the source IPv6-name branch.
